{"id":"p15-l11","minutes":40,"summary":"A robot with more joints than its task needs has a family of poses for every target, and the extra freedom can be spent on a second goal without disturbing the first. You derive the null-space projector I minus J plus J, use it to push joints away from their limits while the tool tracks a circle, see the arm lab’s joint limits make some targets unreachable, and test that the limits are respected only when the null-space term is on.","html":"<h2 id=\"spare-degrees-of-freedom\">Spare degrees of freedom</h2>\n<p>The 3-link planar arm reaching a 2-D point (lesson 07) has one more joint than it needs. Every solution of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6679em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.0556em;\"><span class=\"mord\">˙</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1944em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span></span></span></span> can be written</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8623em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6679em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.0556em;\"><span class=\"mord\">˙</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1944em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9047em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8213em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0713em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8213em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>for any vector <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span></span></span></span>. The matrix <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span></span></span></span> projects onto the <strong>null space</strong> of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span></span></span></span>: joint motions that don’t move the tool at all (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>). For this arm <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> has rank 1, one spare direction: the elbow swinging while the tool stays put, like your own elbow when your hand is on a table.</p>\n<h2 id=\"a-secondary-goal\">A secondary goal</h2>\n<p>Choose <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span></span></span></span> to descend a cost you’d like small. For joint limits, a standard cost is</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.9317em;vertical-align:-1.2777em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-limits\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.8723em;margin-left:0em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.05em;\"></span><span><span class=\"mop op-symbol large-op\">∑</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.2777em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size3\">(</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.2603em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">ma</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">min</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.5678em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˉ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1944em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9721em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size3\">)</span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.654em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.9029em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>zero when every joint is mid-range. Use <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">∇</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span></span></span></span> and the arm drifts away from its limits through the null space, while the first term keeps the tool on track. If the two goals conflict, the tool wins, because the projector removes any part of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span></span></span></span> that would move it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"when-limits-make-targets-unreachable\">When limits make targets unreachable</h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"#lab-arm\">arm lab</a>’s 2-link arm has no spare joint. With its limits on (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7804em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8304em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">180°</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">135°</span></span></span></span>), some points inside the annulus can only be reached by a branch that breaks a limit (lesson 06), and the lab flags them. The 3-link arm’s null space is how a redundant robot keeps more of its workspace usable.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"nullspace\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A 3-link arm with joint limits tracks a circle. Without the null-space term the elbow drifts past its 135 degree limit; switch the term on and the arm reconfigures itself to stay inside every limit while the tool follows the same circle.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>An illustrative arm with links (1.0, 0.8, 0.5) m and limits <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">0°</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">180°</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">135°</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">135°</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">60°</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">60°</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>. The tool tracks a circle of radius 0.4 m centred at (1.2, 0.5) m every 4 s, using resolved-rate control with feedback gain 20:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Pseudo-inverse only: the minimum-norm solution doesn’t care about limits, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> swings between <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">96°</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">149°</span></span></span></span>: 14° past the elbow limit.</li>\n<li>With the null-space term, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0315em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span></span></span></span>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> stays between <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">83°</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">131°</span></span></span></span>, and every joint keeps at least 3.9° from its limits.</li>\n<li>The tracking error is the same with and without the term (under 1 mm, set by the 1 ms integration step), confirming that the null-space motion is invisible at the tool.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">redundancy.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\nL = np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>])                                 <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># illustrative 3-link planar arm (m)</span>\nLIM = np.radians([[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">180</span>], [-<span class=\"hljs-number\">135</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">135</span>], [-<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>]])          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># joint limits</span>\nMID, RNG = LIM.mean(axis=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>), LIM[:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] - LIM[:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">fk</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">q</span>): a = np.cumsum(q); <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array([L @ np.cos(a), L @ np.sin(a)])\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">jac</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">q</span>):\n    a = np.cumsum(q)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array([[-(L[j:] @ np.sin(a[j:])) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> j <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)], [L[j:] @ np.cos(a[j:]) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> j <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)]])\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">limit_cost_grad</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">q</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;H = sum ((q - mid) / range)^2 is smallest mid-range; its gradient pushes joints away from their limits&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * (q - MID) / RNG ** <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">track_circle</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">null_gain, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">8.0</span>, dt=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-3</span>, k=<span class=\"hljs-number\">20.0</span>, centre=(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-number\">1.2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span></span>), radius=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.4</span>, period=<span class=\"hljs-number\">4.0</span></span>):\n    q = np.radians([<span class=\"hljs-number\">70.0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">80.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">40.0</span>])\n    x_start = np.array(centre) + [radius, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _ <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>):                                        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># start on the circle (pseudo-inverse IK)</span>\n        q += np.linalg.pinv(jac(q)) @ (x_start - fk(q))\n    worst_margin, errs, qs = np.inf, [], []\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(T / dt)):\n        w = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi / period; t = i * dt\n        xd = np.array(centre) + radius * np.array([np.cos(w * t), np.sin(w * t)])\n        vd = radius * w * np.array([-np.sin(w * t), np.cos(w * t)])\n        J = jac(q); Jp = np.linalg.pinv(J); N = np.eye(<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>) - Jp @ J\n        qd = Jp @ (vd + k * (xd - fk(q))) + N @ (-null_gain * limit_cost_grad(q))\n        q = q + dt * qd\n        worst_margin = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>(worst_margin, np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>(np.minimum(q - LIM[:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], LIM[:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] - q)))\n        errs.append(np.linalg.norm(xd - fk(q))); qs.append(q.copy())\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.degrees(worst_margin), np.array(errs), np.array(qs)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_null_space_keeps_limits</span>():\n    m0, e0, q0 = track_circle(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>)\n    m1, e1, q1 = track_circle(<span class=\"hljs-number\">10.0</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;pseudo-inverse only : worst limit margin <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{m0:<span class=\"hljs-number\">7.2</span>f}</span> deg (negative = limit broken), q2 range <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.degrees(q0[:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>()):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> to <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.degrees(q0[:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> deg&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;with null-space term: worst limit margin <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{m1:<span class=\"hljs-number\">7.2</span>f}</span> deg, q2 range <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.degrees(q1[:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>()):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> to <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.degrees(q1[:, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>()):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> deg&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;tracking error after 1 s: <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{e0[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> mm and <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{e1[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> mm&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> m0 &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> m1 &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>                                  <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># limits respected only with the null-space term</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> e1[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:].<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-3</span>                              <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># and the tool still tracks the circle</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_null_space_motion_is_invisible</span>():\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(<span class=\"hljs-number\">14</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> q <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> rng.uniform(-<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, (<span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)):\n        J = jac(q); N = np.eye(<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>) - np.linalg.pinv(J) @ J\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(J @ N @ rng.normal(size=<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, atol=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.linalg.matrix_rank(N, tol=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># one spare degree of freedom</span>\n\ntest_null_space_motion_is_invisible()\ntest_null_space_keeps_limits()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Name two other useful secondary goals for the null space.</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Keep away from singularities (climb the manipulability <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span> of lesson 09), avoid an obstacle with the elbow, minimise the gravity torques, or hold a posture that looks natural to people nearby. Several can be stacked in priority order, each projected into the null space of those above it.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does a pure pseudo-inverse controller drift in joint space even when the tool returns to the same point each lap?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The minimum-norm solution is not integrable: following <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8623em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6679em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.0556em;\"><span class=\"mord\">˙</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1944em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span></span></span></span> round a closed path in task space doesn’t generally return to the same joint angles. Each lap leaves the arm in a slightly different elbow pose. The null-space term fixes this by pulling every lap towards the same preferred posture.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p15-l11\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"spare-degrees-of-freedom","title":"Spare degrees of freedom"},{"id":"a-secondary-goal","title":"A secondary goal"},{"id":"when-limits-make-targets-unreachable","title":"When limits make targets unreachable"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p15-l11-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Rank of the null-space projector for a 3-link planar arm with a 2-D position task (away from singularities)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Joints minus task dimensions.</p>\n","answer":1,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p15-l11-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Number of spare degrees of freedom for a 7-joint arm doing a full 6-D pose task?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Like the human arm’s elbow swivel.</p>\n","answer":1,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p15-l11-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>H contribution of a joint at its limit (|q − mid| = half the range)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>((range/2)/range)².</p>\n","answer":0.25,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p15-l11-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>In the worked example, by how many degrees did the pseudo-inverse break the elbow limit?</p>\n","explain":"<p>q2 reached −148.7°.</p>\n","answer":13.7,"tol":0.01,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p15-l11-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>J (I − J⁺J) equals…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Null-space motions don’t move the tool.</p>\n","options":["zero","the identity","J⁺","J"],"answer":0},{"id":"p15-l11-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>If the secondary goal conflicts with the tool task…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Strict priority.</p>\n","options":["they average","the arm stops","the tool task wins, because the projector removes the conflicting part","the secondary goal wins"],"answer":2}],"code":[{"file":"redundancy.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\nL = np.array([1.0, 0.8, 0.5])                                 # illustrative 3-link planar arm (m)\nLIM = np.radians([[0, 180], [-135, 135], [-60, 60]])          # joint limits\nMID, RNG = LIM.mean(axis=1), LIM[:, 1] - LIM[:, 0]\n\ndef fk(q): a = np.cumsum(q); return np.array([L @ np.cos(a), L @ np.sin(a)])\ndef jac(q):\n    a = np.cumsum(q)\n    return np.array([[-(L[j:] @ np.sin(a[j:])) for j in range(3)], [L[j:] @ np.cos(a[j:]) for j in range(3)]])\n\ndef limit_cost_grad(q):\n    \"\"\"H = sum ((q - mid) / range)^2 is smallest mid-range; its gradient pushes joints away from their limits\"\"\"\n    return 2 * (q - MID) / RNG ** 2\n\ndef track_circle(null_gain, T=8.0, dt=1e-3, k=20.0, centre=(1.2, 0.5), radius=0.4, period=4.0):\n    q = np.radians([70.0, -80.0, 40.0])\n    x_start = np.array(centre) + [radius, 0]\n    for _ in range(200):                                        # start on the circle (pseudo-inverse IK)\n        q += np.linalg.pinv(jac(q)) @ (x_start - fk(q))\n    worst_margin, errs, qs = np.inf, [], []\n    for i in range(int(T / dt)):\n        w = 2 * np.pi / period; t = i * dt\n        xd = np.array(centre) + radius * np.array([np.cos(w * t), np.sin(w * t)])\n        vd = radius * w * np.array([-np.sin(w * t), np.cos(w * t)])\n        J = jac(q); Jp = np.linalg.pinv(J); N = np.eye(3) - Jp @ J\n        qd = Jp @ (vd + k * (xd - fk(q))) + N @ (-null_gain * limit_cost_grad(q))\n        q = q + dt * qd\n        worst_margin = min(worst_margin, np.min(np.minimum(q - LIM[:, 0], LIM[:, 1] - q)))\n        errs.append(np.linalg.norm(xd - fk(q))); qs.append(q.copy())\n    return np.degrees(worst_margin), np.array(errs), np.array(qs)\n\ndef test_null_space_keeps_limits():\n    m0, e0, q0 = track_circle(0.0)\n    m1, e1, q1 = track_circle(10.0)\n    print(f\"pseudo-inverse only : worst limit margin {m0:7.2f} deg (negative = limit broken), q2 range {np.degrees(q0[:, 1].min()):.1f} to {np.degrees(q0[:, 1].max()):.1f} deg\")\n    print(f\"with null-space term: worst limit margin {m1:7.2f} deg, q2 range {np.degrees(q1[:, 1].min()):.1f} to {np.degrees(q1[:, 1].max()):.1f} deg\")\n    print(f\"tracking error after 1 s: {e0[1000:].max() * 1000:.3f} mm and {e1[1000:].max() * 1000:.3f} mm\")\n    assert m0 < 0 and m1 > 0                                  # limits respected only with the null-space term\n    assert e1[1000:].max() < 1e-3                              # and the tool still tracks the circle\n\ndef test_null_space_motion_is_invisible():\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(14)\n    for q in rng.uniform(-2, 2, (100, 3)):\n        J = jac(q); N = np.eye(3) - np.linalg.pinv(J) @ J\n        assert np.allclose(J @ N @ rng.normal(size=3), 0, atol=1e-12)\n        assert np.linalg.matrix_rank(N, tol=1e-9) == 1        # one spare degree of freedom\n\ntest_null_space_motion_is_invisible()\ntest_null_space_keeps_limits()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}